{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it","id":509469,"title":"Boston Unveiled: What have you done with it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-09T20:18:41-07:00","id":509469,"title":"Boston Unveiled: What have you done with it?","content":"Hi, everyone! <br /> <br /> In the spirit of sharing and storytelling, what have you done with the Boston supplement? <br /> <br /> Myself, I never ran it, since at the time I felt the Salem Consilium was too much like a kindred princedom to my liking. Maybe it was the presentation, I don't know, it just felt that despite the excellent ideas contained, I wouldn't know where to start. Eventually the mage line started to show its strengths and along came some powerful fiction pieces too, that finally let me grok BU. The real authority in Boston wasn't the Consilium itself, but the Secret Concord: all else was secondary to that unholy alliance of ruthless witches and christian powermongers. Once I started to contemplate the idea of filling the setting with a few more cabals and some 2ed caucus structures, the ideas started to flow again.<br /> <br /> Did any of you expanded the material presented to include other supernatural societies? Did any of you changed parts of the setting-as-written? Have you found any difficulty introducing a particular element of the setting? What about adapting the setting to the 2nd edition new rules and setting changes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T11:45:22-07:00","id":510076,"title":"","content":"Alright, so I've been designing a multi-splat Chronicle for the past couple of months. It's basically a mash-up of Boston Unveiled (which has made my world-building work SO much easier) and the older Dark Colonies stuff, with lots of local history thrown in. Mages control most of Boston, vampires control what's left, there's a changeling freehold in Waltham, and sin-eaters and werewolves cooperate over various disaster sites to mend damage done both in Twilight and the Shadow Realm (the Tewksbury Explosion, the Pemberton Mill collapse, the Great Revere Train Wreck, and what-have-you). Virtually all of the BU history is intact, as are most of the cabals introduced.<br /> <br /> I've kneecapped the Illuminated Pentad though. I remember reading a couple of stories about the Nemean possessing Thanatos of the Pentad, spying on a Pentad-rallied conspirators meeting to overthrow him, and then siccing a bunch of monsters on them. He then gets stuck in his own mind by the rest of the Silver Ladder for his transgressions. I tweaked it some, so it results in the Nemean never getting punished. Now, a sole survivor from the Pentad yanks the players around for the eventual end goal of assassinating the Nemean.<br /> <br /> On that note, I'm running with a lot of the Red Word stuff. I knew I wanted some kind of over-arching doom plot that all roads eventually lead toward. I'm not running with the Bleached Schooner or the Austere Stone of Gilead, as this campaign is complicated enough without having to design MORE separate societies. I'm still on the fence about the Wood of Empty Houses and Beast of Burden.<br /> <br /> I'm also running with the Tremere elements out of Dorchester. I'm not sure I like Mama Desta as an antagonist, given the weird breast-feeding child soul theft thing and how it will definitely weird out my players? I pulled Madeline Coventry from Dark Colonies, and she'll be running around Dorchester with Desta at her side as a heavy instead.<br /> <br /> I uhhhh have not read any of the Mage-specific 2e stuff. I can't really answer questions about it. :\\ Hopefully I'll be able to run First Night sometime later this month, and then the first game sometime after that. Some of my players are super-psyched, and some other folks I've bounced ideas off of want to guest-ST as NPCs. It's the first time I've ever done anything remotely like STing or DMing. It'll either be great or a total disaster! I have high hopes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5236-lackey-man-ren","name":"Lackey Man Ren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T12:36:01-07:00","id":510106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> all else was secondary to that unholy alliance of ruthless witches and christian powermongers. </div> </div> </div>The problem I have is, it's not really clear how that authority actually works. The Nemean does wilfully stupid and harsh things (such as blocking a cabal from moving into Boston) and the characters just accept it, despite the Nemean not really having the firepower to back up his claims. If a player defies the Nemean, what exactly can he do? Send his three sentinels after them? Mobilise the consilium that hates his guts? Even the White Putnams don't seem like they'd really be any help. I get that it's meant to be that kind of arrangement so that the players can up end the setting but it does feel a bit odd when NPCs acquiesce to threats that clearly have nothing backing them.<br /> <br /> The other thing I'd look at is the Shadow Chorus. They're pretty cool, but their handling of the GotV caucus is dreadful from the perspective of the order book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T13:46:02-07:00","id":510161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=510106#post510106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem I have is, it's not really clear how that authority actually works. The Nemean does wilfully stupid and harsh things (such as blocking a cabal from moving into Boston) and the characters just accept it, despite the Nemean not really having the firepower to back up his claims. If a player defies the Nemean, what exactly can he do? Send his three sentinels after them? Mobilise the consilium that hates his guts? Even the White Putnams don't seem like they'd really be any help. I get that it's meant to be that kind of arrangement so that the players can up end the setting but it does feel a bit odd when NPCs acquiesce to threats that clearly have nothing backing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about the Nemean is that he doesn't seem to need any back-up? In the Silver Ladder book, he sneaks into a secret let's-overthrow-the-Hierarch meeting INSIDE one of the conspirators and proceeds to raise enough hell that people lose limbs. I mean, the rest of the Silver Ladder busts him for being a douche in a treaty zone, but the point is the dude is scary enough to compel people to not openly move against him.<br /> <br /> When I get around to having him in a scene, I'm playing him like a crazier Ridcully from Pratchett's Discworld. Seems like such a good fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5236-lackey-man-ren","name":"Lackey Man Ren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T14:33:20-07:00","id":510200,"title":"","content":"Yeah the Nemean is a scary guy and he has some other scary guys who back him up, like The Ax.<br /> <br /> Honestly, if you are a bunch of regular Mages who turn up on his turf unwelcomed, then the Nemean is not the type to get huffy and sent some diplomats etc. He'll just take some guys and go around to your Sanctum and fuck you up. He'll put bodies in the ground and not think twice about it. Remember, power does not equal the brutality needed to exercise that against another living, breathing, feeling person. The Nemean is plenty powerful, and plenty brutal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T14:34:37-07:00","id":510201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but the point is the dude is scary enough to compel people to not openly move against him. </div> </div> </div>I just don't think he is. He's one guy, and even masters can die very easily. If he's terrorising the consilium, he needs a structure to do that through.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think it's an insumountable issue, I just don't think it's explained properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T15:59:14-07:00","id":510217,"title":"","content":"I think Dave made the point that Boston is supposed to be a Consilium in a fail-state, and that the Nemean's dickishness has a purpose revealed in one of the fictions.<br /> <br /> Masters of Life are pretty scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T16:46:24-07:00","id":510239,"title":"","content":"I believe it's heavily implied, if not stated outright, in the Silver Ladder book that the Nemean acts like a violently unstable tyrant for a reason. He wants to create an environment where the mages in his Consilium are eventually forced to overthrow and replace him, ideally with someone wiser and more capable as Hierarch.<br /> <br /> At least, that was the original intent...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T17:08:10-07:00","id":510253,"title":"","content":"I definitely recall that but can't recall why he wants to do that.<br /> <br /> Also I recall that he speaks to the Old Man on the edge of the Ocean Ourbouros (or however that's spelt) and goes inside his Hut but cannot recall if he tricks him or is tricked or whatever. I do think he has become an Archmage at that point, though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T17:18:01-07:00","id":510257,"title":"","content":"The Nemean is deliberately trying to provoke people into deposing him. The assumption being that whoever does will be a player character -- he's there so your PCs can beat him up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T17:18:05-07:00","id":510258,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It depends at what point you are at in his story. <br /> <br /> By the end, he is an Aswadim. His role in the Secret Accord was to be the Baron of the Prince of 100,000, who was the 3rd signatory of their treaty. He was in the process of crossing his threshold when the Silver Ladder trapped him, and thus managed to escape. The Nemean seen in the story involving the Khonshu, whose life is being seized by an Archmage, is an Ochema. He is continuing his role as the Baron as an Archmage. <br /> <br /> <br /> As for why he messed things up, I can only guess:<br /> -It is quite possible that the state he created in Boston was part of his attempt to begin his Seeking. It would fit a Thyrsus who styles himself the Nemean: create a cut throat environment which favors the strong and punishes the weak, the Lion only surrendering his &quot;pride&quot; when defeated. But that is just a guess. <br /> <br /> -They also have him confronting his past self, so that could have been another part of his seeking. Archmages are wierd like that.<br /> <br /> -Or it could be that the Concord required that the two cabals had to retain power. Essentially, an exit clause if the Prince failed his end. I am sure there were caveats that the cabals couldn't surrender power or self-terminate. So it is possible the Nemean was trying to get out of the deal by having the other cabals remove the Noose and Putnams from power, but couldn't just step aside. And he failed, getting himself deposed but remaining the Prince's Baron.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that was all I managed to suss out from the Anthology, Dave's post, the fluff from books and how IM describes seeking and Archmastery. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 05-10-2015, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T17:25:17-07:00","id":510262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=510258#post510258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">He is an Aswadim. His role in the Secret Accord was to be the Baron of the Prince of 100,000, who was the 3rd signatory of their treaty. He was in the process of crossing his threshold when the Silver Ladder trapped him, and thus managed to escape. The Nemean seen in the story involving the mage (name escapes me)whose life is being seized by an Archmage is an Ochema. He is continuing his role as the Baron as an Archmage.<br /> <br /> It is quite possible that the state he created in Boston was part of his attempt to begin his Seeking. It would fit a Thyrsus who styles himself the Nemean: create a cut throat environment which favors the strong and punishes the weak, the Lion only surrendering his &quot;pride&quot; when defeated. But that is just a guess. They also have him confronting his past self, so that could have been another part of his seeking. Archmages are wierd like that.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the story about Khonshu, the Obrimos... I want to say Mysterium? guy who gets mixed up with all manner of madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T17:39:58-07:00","id":510268,"title":"","content":"Yep! Thats the guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T15:02:49-07:00","id":511190,"title":"","content":"I know about the Nemean being a plot device (for want of a better word). Malcolm said so years ago. I would also add, my original post said I know. That's not what my issue is.<br /> <br /> My problem is about the structure of his authority and getting a picture in my head of how he actually exerts his political influence. I need a coherent way to present him so it doesn't look like the NPCs are just kowtowing to him because the plot says so. When the PCs decide to defy the Noose, what does the Nemean do? More importantly, how do the major cabals react? Presumably, they should back him up because for whatever reason they\u2019re a part of his power structure. But those reasons aren\u2019t terribly clear.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t really buy him beating people personally, I mean, he gets unlucky once and he could easily end up dead. Seems unlikely to me. Plus, it seems heavily suggested that he rules in part through legal means. He abuses his authority, but he holds that authority legitimately; and others in the setting at least grudgingly acknowledge that authority as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T15:17:53-07:00","id":511209,"title":"","content":"Remember how a Master of Spirit can establish their own courts of which they are the top dog, and can create their own monsters? That's some pretty sweet backup to have when you go in with your physical stats jacked up and a nice regeneration spell on you while you're in the shape of a giant lion with inpenetrable skin and claws of bronze.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T16:01:50-07:00","id":511274,"title":"","content":"I didn't say the guy wasn't a badass, I mean, he has 4 dots in weaponry, he's clearly been in a fight or two. I just don't think the Hierarch would be personally enforcing his own rule in that way. It's still dangerous, and as Hierarch he should have better options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T16:24:07-07:00","id":511287,"title":"","content":"He does. He has the Ax (amongst other Sentinels), he has a strong power base in the form of his own cabal, by virtue of his very position and resources he can bully and bribe others into doing what he says and victimising those who he takes a dislike to, and he's also got various spirit servants he can send to do his bidding. So he does have plenty of options outside of dealing with things personally, though he totally can deal with things personally (and often does).<br /> <br /> Even outside of his own personal ability to kick the shit out of people he doesn't like, he has plenty of other options. And the fact that he is so willing to go straight to violence if displeased creates perhaps one of his greatest weapons; fear. People are scared of the Nemean (not without reason, it's not like he doesn't back up his threats), and he uses that against them very effectively. He's very good at being a Tyrant, that's for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T16:37:56-07:00","id":511299,"title":"","content":"I have to imagine that, at least by the presentation of First Edition, it is not unfeasable to have hierarchs be a bit hands on, because the Boston Consilium consists of a good seventy people. I mean, himself, a couple member of his cabal, his three sentinels, that's close to 10% of the entire population, and probably at least equal in size (and almost always superior in magical heft) to anybody he'd be throwing.his weight against because you're never going to have the entire Consilium unified against him; you're barely going to have two or three cabals working together (those mystagogues with the oath bound Arrows don't really seem to care, when they're not holding themselves as so above it all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T21:56:49-07:00","id":511658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=510257#post510257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nemean is deliberately trying to provoke people into deposing him. The assumption being that whoever does will be a player character -- he's there so your PCs can beat him up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhhhhhh...! That's a lot simpler than the conclusion I came to. I was under the impression he <i>had</i> to keep the Boston Consilium in chaos, but was also actively working against those who would depose him. I thought that if Boston mages started cooperating and knocked either the Ebon Noose or the White Putnams from power that it might've set off a weird clause in the Secret Concord, much like Freemind posited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5236-lackey-man-ren","user":"Lackey Man Ren","date":". 05-12-2015, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5236-lackey-man-ren","name":"Lackey Man Ren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T21:10:22-07:00","id":517619,"title":"","content":"As presented in Boston Unveiled, the Nemean has a fairly large apparatus to enforce his rule. He has the Ebon Noose, the biggest cabal in the consillium, as well the Gravediggers, and entire cabal of dedicated assassins/warriors under his command. In addition to that, the White Putnams support him in everything. Then the council has also let him appoint most of the &quot;police force&quot; of the consillium, which are the ones who are doing most of the enforcing of the rules. So something like 20 of the mages are there to help him enforce his will, a direct conflict with him involves picking a fight with them. As long as the rest of the mages are disorganized and insular, it makes ok sense for the biggest group to be able to boss everone around. If everyone else bands together, then he looses, but until then he is king.<br /> <br /> I never got around to doing much with Boston back in my last game, but once 2nd comes around I am returning to Boston with a small group. I am thinking a lot about how to change or update Boston to run it in the new edition. Looks like I am going to be running a game where two disciple-level Guardians arrive in Boston, coming under the command of the Shadow Chorus and pursuing the goals of the guardians in the consillium.<br /> <br /> So a related question to &quot;what have you done with it?&quot; would be &quot;how would you change/update Boston?&quot;, both for the new edition and also just based on what worked and what didn't.<br /> <br /> The things I am thinking about are...<br /> Making it more clear/focused what the central mystery of Boston is and how it draws mages in. I know that it is the Secret Concord, but how do mages get involved in that? I think I would bring the particular qualities of the astral in Boston into focus as well, as something that attracts mages. Maybe expand on the combat zone, as an area of interest. Make sure that some of the cabals are dedicated to exploring those things. Still, the concord is cool, but it is hard to see how mages investigate it, get involved with it, when it's so deadly and there's almost no way to investigate it, without trying to turn members of the tyrant's or his friends' cabals into informers.<br /> <br /> Advancing the whole Nemean storyline - dunno how interesting it is to run a game about toppling the old Hierarch, especially since mages have to be powerful and/or well-established to do it. Very long-term. So how would a Boston on the edge of disposing the Nemean look, how would Boston look after the Nemean has just been ousted? Who could actually do it in the setting? Who would be an interesting new Hierarch?<br /> <br /> The Free Council of Boston has always annoyed me. Their order chapter in the book talks about democrats, libertines and revolutionaries, but the libertines of Boston are pirates and borderline apostates. None of them are doing anything politically, all of them are just playing around or delving into some personal thing... or being hippies in the most passive way possible. How to shatter that? I think part of the point is them is that after destroying the Emerald Scroll they lost their purpose and have just been becoming more and more inactive and powerless since then... with the loss of a common enemy and purpose. Still, I like the council with an edge, so how would they be changed for a new edition?<br /> <br /> So what about you guys? How would you change the things I mention above? Or do you think there are more important/interesting things to change around? There's also the fact that a decade (more or less) has passed since the book came out, how should the setting change to reflect that? Not necessarily advance the setting by 8 years, but perhaps reimagining things a bit to include more recent events (more marathon bombing, less big dig, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2206,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2206-suicide-king","user":"Suicide King","date":". 05-18-2015, 12:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2206-suicide-king","name":"Suicide King","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:05:20-07:00","id":518470,"title":"","content":"You know, rereading Boston, it actually does go into more detail of how the Nemeans reigme actually works than I'd thought it did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T05:01:39-07:00","id":521680,"title":"","content":"Me, I've used BU as support for one story of my Mage chronicle. <br /> <br /> A PC mysterium censor is sent to Boston to &quot;acquire&quot; the sinister artifacts of one &quot;Ahriman&quot;. The investigation leads to a forceful confrontation and the PC killing Ahriman in self-defense with a vulgar Death curse, not before becoming tainted with the abyssal artifacts contained in his personal sanctum. Meanwhile, the rest of the PCs come looking for his missing cabalmate and indulge in a bit of politics with the White Putnams and a short fight with some Red Word cultists.<br /> <br /> A month later, Chain Parris returns the favor by visiting some of the PCs at their home back at Portland (actually a fictitious Portland-equivalent, long story). Cue the Red Cult killing in their home turf, a creepy wooden statue of a creature not of this world sent by a &quot;Mr Mark Long&quot; for a museum exhibit in the city and the Seers of the Throne trying to avert a sinister prophecy. The PCs find out about the Blasphemous Scribe, kill all cultists and wizards involved (some in cold blood) and swear a pact of silence to avoid strengthening the Prince. Chain goes back to Boston, and just when the Ebon Noose starts to figure out what happened with Ahriman, the Convocation kidnaps The Nemean, putting the Noose mages in confusion and disarray.<br /> <br /> Three months later, and the Noose is ready for payback, with Anacaona in command. The PCs have been forewarned about something nasty coming their way, but they have no idea the kind of shitstorm the Noose is about to release on them.<br /> <br /> So, while I'm preparing a potential Boston game, there are some changes that are going to happen if the PCs don't intervene, partly inspired by the now-defunct chat mage venues and some ideas of my own:<br /> <br /> * The Council is just a big farce right now, deadlocked in voting for the next Hierarch between Numa and Potestas in one hand and Anacaona and Parris in the other. Hydra hasn't left her mansion since her defeat at the hands of the Ax. The Gravediggers are only answering to the Hierarch, not the Ebon Noose. All parties are getting ready for open hostilities if any other party makes a wrong move.<br /> <br /> * The Convocation names Khumeia the new Deacon, but shortly afterwards she will lose her mind and will kill a few apostates and Consilium mages with vulgar magic in open street. Thanatos is still in intensive care after the failed coup against the Hierarch and Faustina will wisely leave Boston, presumably for New Haven.<br /> <br /> * The Dead Wrens lose the Emerald Scroll to a magical fire provoked by the Shadow Chorus, and they lay low in a safehouse down the harbor, while they reorganize and plan revenge. Eventually they will stage a heist against the Shadow Chorus' sanctum that will end in blood and horror for both parties.<br /> <br /> * SMG have created a magical software that can predict where a hallow is most likely to appear in the Great Boston area and they plan to hold an open auction at the regional Assembly to earn big money, artifacts, and convince other libertines to move to the area. This will backfire when Scorpio shows up, spoiling for a fight. If they defeat the Seers and the software works, however, SMG's actions will provoke a flood of new mages arriving in Boston, Harvard and Salem, and no small amount of conflict with the more established cabals.<br /> <br /> I'm using three more cabals to flesh the Consilium up:<br /> <br /> * The Broncinean Tripod of Ophidian Logic exists and has fought against the Red Word cult, though right now they are wounded and laying low, protected by Aurem and struggling with their own abyssal tainting.<br /> <br /> * Solon's Witnesses is an all-female, mostly Guardians new cabal that throws its support for a Guardian Councilor, but nobody knows if that means the Shadow Chorus, her own cabal or someone else entirely.<br /> <br /> * Franklyn Hill is a gang-style libertine column that is carving its home turf right below Vision's nose, fighting a shadow war in the streets against the Company.<br /> <br /> All of that may or may not appear in my game, depending on a series of factors. I'll go along with what my players throw me, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> In a slightly unrelated note, what's the reading order for all the stories involving The Nemean and the rest of the Boston Consilium? <br /> I've gathered the following:<br /> - Mysterium: &quot;Censorious&quot;<br /> - Silver Ladder: &quot;The Cage is the Lion's Heart&quot;<br /> - Left-Hand Path: &quot;The Veil, Nothing More&quot;<br /> - FWC Anthology: &quot;The Unmurdered Man&quot;<br /> - FWC Anthology: &quot;The Human Heart&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T06:48:28-07:00","id":521801,"title":"","content":"The Nemean has personal power and alliances at his command, but he doesn't actually interfere much with Boston except to protect the area from significant dangers and enrich his junta-like cabal in an occasional, opportunistic fashion. So in Boston mages actually have a bit more freedom than they might in places where the Consilium is more proactive. You want to rip off another cabal? Go for it. Nobody wants to get the Hierarch involved so you'll either get away with it, or it'll get settled via duel or backroom shenanigans. Boston has/had a bastard in charge, but it's also the place where the Free Council can run a bar any sorcerer can show up at without being screwed around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T06:51:06-07:00","id":521804,"title":"","content":"The story order should be:<br /> <br /> - Mysterium: &quot;Censorious&quot;<br /> - Silver Ladder: &quot;The Cage is the Lion's Heart&quot;<br /> - Left-Hand Path: &quot;The Veil, Nothing More&quot;<br /> - FWC Anthology: &quot;The Human Heart&quot;<br /> - FWC Anthology: &quot;The Unmurdered Man&quot;<br /> <br /> With the last two it's possible to read them the other way around. It should be noted, however, that the Nemean isn't really an archmage. He didn't *quite* get there, which is why he can screw around on Earth.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T16:42:06-07:00","id":522668,"title":"","content":"I think the reaction to the setup in Boston really shows the difference between readers and players. I designed Boston for play. When people approach Boston that way they get a great deal out of it. When they want the book to be something to read about an archetypal/typical city, it's not as useful. Fact is, none of the three original signature cities are really typical.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's deliberately unstable with an antagonist front and center. At the time, it was also written to make a clean break with Ascension, where the Traditions are an alliance pointed at a greater goal. Consilii aren't &quot;alliances.&quot; They're governments that exist out of the need to limit violence between groups that may not have common objectives at all. Consilli aren't your friend. They're not vampire courts either, because mage society isn't feudal and isn't concerned with managing &quot;herd&quot; access. So mage claims an entirely different place than its predecessor or other games. Let's say that for people with . . . less expansive imaginations . . . it was easier to not read it and mentally paste in shit from other games than to read it and run with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T17:34:16-07:00","id":522715,"title":"","content":"I think Boston accomplishes that goal rather well. Out of curiosity, do you feel that interpretation of the Consilium as a concept is still true in the 2nd Edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T20:33:42-07:00","id":522855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=522715#post522715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Boston accomplishes that goal rather well. Out of curiosity, do you feel that interpretation of the Consilium as a concept is still true in the 2nd Edition?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well it depends on the state of Boston. The stories advance a plot but the game doesn't really do metaplot. So the question of what Boston looks like after the Nemean is optional, though 2e assumes he's no longer Hierarch. The Ebon Noose is still strong and the Putnams still have influence that bridges Awakened and Sleepers. It could be an interesting situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T02:46:13-07:00","id":523062,"title":"","content":"I think he was referring to the line about government out of the need to limit violence between groups that may not have common objectives, rather than Boston specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T02:47:08-07:00","id":523063,"title":"","content":"At risk of derailing this thread, I think BU reads different with the right context. Reading it as a first supplement may have left the reader with the feeling of the book not explaining enough; reading it after Sanctum &amp; Sigil and Guardians of the Veil is a completely different story. Reading it now after all these years worth of supplements, well...<br /> <br /> The core book at the time suffered IMHO of presentation problems. I remember having a really hard time picturing a default consilium in my head, something that hadn't happened with VtR or WtF. So, while it's true none of the Big Three had a &quot;normal&quot; setting supplement, BU may have suffered the most as an early supplement inadvertedly tasked with filling the gaps left by the core book.<br /> <br /> Personally speaking, it was the Boston short stories that rekindled my interest for BU and made me buy the book after an initial dismissal. Those were the stories that I enjoyed the most, so that's a praise for Mr Sheppard here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T03:55:24-07:00","id":523078,"title":"","content":"I found the opposite. I think the book benefits from reading it as it is rather than trying to retroactively insert later supliments into it. Some stuff works fine (the Guanxi stuff from Mysterium is great), but stuff like the way the caucus' work is basically irrelevant for anyone other than the Mysterium and maybe the Arrow; and I think it would suffer as a setting from trying to force it to fit those patterns too closely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T06:41:37-07:00","id":523132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=523062#post523062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he was referring to the line about government out of the need to limit violence between groups that may not have common objectives, rather than Boston specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e shifts the emphasis to Convocations. Consilii still perform the role of settling disputes and delivering collective justice, but Convocations deal with larger issues. You might go to one if a Consilium proves to be totally useless in dealing with your magic zoning dispute, but the Convocation would probably deal with it as a structural problem with that Consilium, leaving your actual problem to be settled by any directive. It might not go down this way, since much depends on the actual scenario.<br /> <br /> It should be noted that it takes a lot for a Consilium to be thought of as a failure. Remember that Awakened are capable of governing themselves through oaths, duels and exercising the Great Rights. Failure happens when mages don't do these things and the Consilium doesn't fix this, or the Consilium doesn't effectively respond to threats to the whole. In Boston, the Consilium under the Nemean was effective at making it a very bad idea to break rules, because the punishment for doing that was having to deal with the Consilium. Mages there mostly governed themselves. It was ineffective at dealing with collective threats because of overfed self-interest, the Consilium's lack of proactivity and its focus on one big problem in the form of the Secret Concord. But even the Nemean knew that maybe somebody should do something about rampaging cannibals and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":164,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","user":"Malcolm","date":". 05-21-2015, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T08:17:53-07:00","id":523264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=523132#post523132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be noted that it takes a lot for a Consilium to be thought of as a failure. Remember that Awakened are capable of governing themselves through oaths, duels and exercising the Great Rights. Failure happens when mages don't do these things and the Consilium doesn't fix this, or the Consilium doesn't effectively respond to threats to the whole. In Boston, the Consilium under the Nemean was effective at making it a very bad idea to break rules, because the punishment for doing that was having to deal with the Consilium. Mages there mostly governed themselves. It was ineffective at dealing with collective threats because of overfed self-interest, the Consilium's lack of proactivity and its focus on one big problem in the form of the Secret Concord. But even the Nemean knew that maybe somebody should do something about rampaging cannibals and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I myself always liked how Boston portrayed the usual pulp version of New England secret politics as a collection of Colonialist Old Money and preppy Ivy League scum bags with a few slum lords sprinkled on top and saying &quot;this is actually something functional&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T13:43:43-07:00","id":523676,"title":"","content":"I ran a single player Boston chronicle, taking an established character from another game and inserting them into the Ebon Noose. It didn\u2019t feel like there was any better way to touch on the Secret Concord. The book felt unclear on ways to explore that mystery \u2014 just a few side bars here and there. My twist was that the third signatory was a cruel Ananke created by an archmaster who survived his time in Epona\u2019s Chariot, seeking to undo the dread summoning of the Blasphemous Scribe. <br /> <br /> It is a very interesting setting, but it does not seem easy to run at first glance. I felt like I had to do a lot of digging to get a good feel for how everything works together. More than a few NPCs are compelling and can carry stories if fleshed out. Ferrum, for instance, has a lot of potential. He is already an Adamant Sage at a relatively young age. There is some natural conflict with the death of his brother and a growing rift between his cabal and the Brotherhood. In my chronicle, the player mediated a release of the Knights from their vows of service, so that Ferrum would become a Councilor. If the Nemean is waiting for a Sage to defeat him, I think Ferrum would be the most likely NPC to be able to do so, though he might need to be nudged by a PC out of his ennui. <br /> <br /> The Grey Pope and his Pylon makes a terrifying antagonist. His write-up was done before the Seers were fleshed out, which makes it difficult to get a good grasp on how all the Seers are operating. The Consilium\u2019s leaders are based more in Northern Massachusetts than Boston, and the Asylum is a likely obstacle for cabals looking to move the power base south.<br /> <br /> The Leon family would be nice to see more of, as it hints at a large group of sleepwalkers and Proximi, as well as an entire spirit court under their control, judging by Numa\u2019s rotes. My player took an immediate liking to the family, and their creepy antiquated notions of arranged marriages, so I had that tied to an ongoing plot about the Guardians of the Veil\u2019s past dabbling in eugenics.<br /> <br /> Overall, the setting has a nice libertarian feel with regards to the consilium structure. Other mages are not going to snoop into your business too much, but it will be hard to get help for your problems if you don\u2019t have something to offer. Even tackling a problem by having an NPC do something for you will lead to another conflict to enrich the story. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d be interested to see this setting updated for Mage 2e, given that there is a focus more on the various order caucuses. Some caucuses seem lacking compared to how the cabals are described. There are only three Guardians of the Veil in the consilium (Culsu, Februs, and Hades) but there seems to be enough unnamed solitaries in the area to call a caucus to order. It would be great to see these communities fleshed out, and have some brief descriptions on their interactions with neighboring out-of-state cities like Providence, Rhode Island.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4725-murder_of_craws","name":"Murder_of_Craws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4725_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T10:47:02-07:00","id":539723,"title":"","content":"(Forgive my quick rambling that I can't spend overly much time on b/c of more pressing obligations, but I felt compelled to opine.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=522668#post522668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the reaction to the setup in Boston really shows the difference between readers and players. I designed Boston for play. When people approach Boston that way they get a great deal out of it. When they want the book to be something to read about an archetypal/typical city, it's not as useful. Fact is, none of the three original signature cities are really typical.</div> </div> </div> </div>This statement is a little (unintentionally) disingenuous as it sets up a false dichotomy between those who read vs. those who play. Many of us read with the intent of integrating those disparate pieces into a framework with which we can visualize and determine the appropriate reactions in play. After all, it's incredibly awkward to have a player highlight an inconsistency or point of order that conflicts with or possibly derails the &quot;narrative-in-process&quot;. I've seen it happen to others, and definitely wouldn't want to be the subject of it! Thus, any anomalies that intersects with our gaming plans/planning can become sources of grating consternation that, if unresolvable via heuristics (or worse, complicated by) can lead to the collapse of a game/gaming opportunity, stress, etc.<br /> <br /> Granted, this player vs. reader idea is also entwined with the idea of the Boston being an atypical consilium within the super-setting of Awakening. (And being ditto for other lines' settings.) Yet again, many people are looking for an example to build their own games from - so of course they're going to look at the one official example given for ideas, inspiration and/or baselines... in hopes of playing.<br /> ---<br /> <br /> Instead of a division b/t gamers and readers, perhaps the split that Malcolm is referring to is a spectrum of analytical vs. ... archetypical? At the extremes you have those who OCDly require internal consistency vs. those who just don't care. Or, close to something that could be of use in reasonable discourse (or at least its casual cousin), people who find enough internal consistency in archetypes, conflicts and motion (and are fine with hand waving away in-setting paradoxes for a variety of reasons, not exclusive of: It's just a game, &quot;cinematographical&quot; or short story influence vs. novels or technical documents, not having cringe reflexes to deus ex machina or 'just cause' reasoning for occurrences, reactions, etc., being prone to improv vs. structured plotting, and more.)<br /> <br /> [Note: I am not deriding the latter pole, especially since they're probably the happier of the two lots. I wouldn't doubt that anxiety, perfectionism and other neuroses drive folks like myself towards the first notion, thus forcing us to waste a lot of time and heartache over minutia, instead of just having fun. At least to a certain extent. YMMV,. Plus, it's just an unvetted brainfart... err, theory.]<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Of course, we who regularly over-think things often fail at recognizing that (in this specific case) a privileged perch produced our pedantic proscriptions - hindsight. Not all inconsistencies within the supplement were born of reticence, carelessness, or worse - intent. Nor could the authors have Guardians of the Veil or Summoners (etc.) on hand to pull from/check against. Awakening as a platform was still inchoate. Facts are provided from a set of assumptions that either didn't have design-consensus or were still evolving within the creative crucible. &quot;Water colors&quot; are employed where the material touches on these aspects. Loose, blurry but enough to carry a definitive sense. (ex: Orders &amp; Titles)<br /> <br /> Other causes of consternation are rooted in conflicts or concepts that lost prominence or changed by degrees. One example is the whole &quot;Boston Consilium ruled from Salem&quot; thing, but the Consilium comprises member cabals in Gloucester, Cambridge, and possibly more. Or the weird Chain Parris choosing to be a mystagogue being taken as a sign of some sort of acquiesence to the Nemean's control (as opposed to rebellion) and w/little other discourse as to the qualities he or the order possessed which brought the two together. And yet his *thearch* cabalmates think he's upholding the status quo, but want to leave the consilium. Or how the Putnams reconcile religion/Christianity's mandate for humility w/Thearch ideology. (Heck, I'm willing to bet that the only reason the Nemean is a thearch instead of an Arrow is b/c 'ladders lead' - since the Arrows in his cabal have no qualms with emulating him.) Or why the Gravediggers are oathsworn assassins to the Hiearch/Noose(iirc) or whatever. Or the dearth of discourse on the Wampanoag/Algonquin/etc. expression of Atlantis/Diamond/Seers, compared to the myriad material hinting at sleeper-culture/truths-rooted divisions trumping Pentacle. Or the Lex &amp; Gold Laws. Or all the proximi/-like running around. The minimal/implied Seer pyramid of pylons being regional (if not municipal) vs. regional (and the sole ministry represented being (the only ministry mentioned?) in the core book.<br /> <br /> Exacerbating the kinks induced by by being on the wrong side of Awakening's maturation is the simple fact that, let's face it, some details/decisions just needed to be made and numbers needed to be rounded out- and coming up with a cast of cabals is much tougher than, say, kindred luminaries. . Like the Chaplain confusion, the Noose's weird lack of a potent acanthus; the lackluster libertine lineup; the Shadow Chorus having two mystagogue members for whatever reason. Or how Arathnos and/or Thanatos ever got into the Silver Ladder. Hades and his Wisdom 8. Hydra. Thanatos. Silentium. Or the lack of historical cabal rosters despite the supposed big deal of certain cabal's longevity. Like to the Nemean's predecessor, who is likely a thearch magister - or better yet, the Ebon Noose's lack of any one belonging to the cabal prior to the Nemean's rise to leadership. (Tiamat and Ahriman are refugees from other cabals circa the 90s? Then the Ax. The rest are basically newbs. That's ~ 30 years of the Nemean, the guy he replaced and ... ??? The Putnams have a similar quirk revolving around .. Jonas(?) but not mentioning Chain's predecessor, or etc.)<br /> <br /> But I digress... and I'm sure I'm missing/misremembering a lot, too. The important point is, the root of a lot of the confusion is the natural disadvantage of coming out at the front end of a platform doesn't nail its essential non-mechanical particulars down prior to release. With the exception of certain decisions whose wisdom eludes me/I respectfully disagree with, I'm willing to bet that if the setting was being fleshed out for the first time at the back end of Awakening 1.0, a lot of those prickly particulars arising from the details would never have been. (I'm seeing the Putnams as a GoV/Hieromagus-leaning aparatus, an Ebon Noose whose initial protectorate dictate leads to its sublimation from community oriented / atoning SLs to rugged frontiersmen AAs who think true strength comes from independence or somesuch (or alternatively, pulling together &amp; emphasizing two bits the Ebon Noose's background flavor text: namely it being a loose confederation of cabals and its being whispered by some of Salem's occultists - make it a Cryptopoly under the management of a pseudo-lineage succession cabal(s)/alliance; Native American themed elements like lost temples/outposts/rando gold laws, Raptor-pylon-cults; maybe even aligning or preluding the Nameless Wars with 1776-1812 somehow - could maybe make a better tale for a more thematic uprooting of the Stone Assembly; and a lot more Paternoster. Reworking the Pentad's ingress into Boston involing a proximi-bloodline-maintenance courting-like-b/t Khumeia &amp; Numa's broods. Certainly, at some point there could be some toying with that weird alternate Scales of whatnot governing option in either the ancient, pre-colonial or post-revolution eras. Maybe adjusting the red word away from the time-stuff and more towards the idea of the bounds of a sleeping hunger being loosened when the Tri-Hill or whatever area was filled in and disrupted the ley lines.<br /> <br /> ... ugh, must stop digressing. NOT ENOUGH TIME!<br /> ---<br /> Also, finally, as a Boston-native, I'd really appreciate it if people stopped using the acronym BU to refer to Boston Unveiled <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, since - in the context of the city/state that the text encompasses! - BU is short for Boston University. Embarrassment <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/793-phil","name":"phil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:21:58-07:00","id":541144,"title":"","content":"@Phil, my long and insightful post replying to some of your ideas was unfortunately eaten by a forum bug, so I'll just say: I mostly agree with your observations. / I thank you for your keen eye in finding all those little inconsistencies and potential setting gaps that could be filled or bent to update the setting to 2nd Ed. / I didn't know about the BU acronym already standing for Boston University; it's a trivia nugget for me, so thanks amyway and apologies.<br /> <br /> I'm still brainstorming and riffing off ideas out of what you have been seeding in this thread, and I'll come back later with a more coherent &quot;updated Boston Unveiled&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T03:40:47-07:00","id":542422,"title":"","content":"A lot of those points aren't kinks, they're just decisions you don't like. The Nemean being Thearch and not an Arrow for example, makes perfect sense in terms of the two order books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T09:40:23-07:00","id":547170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=541144#post541144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Phil, my long and insightful post replying to some of your ideas was unfortunately eaten by a forum bug, so I'll just say: I mostly agree with your observations. / I thank you for your keen eye in finding all those little inconsistencies and potential setting gaps that could be filled or bent to update the setting to 2nd Ed. / I didn't know about the BU acronym already standing for Boston University; it's a trivia nugget for me, so thanks amyway and apologies.<br /> <br /> I'm still brainstorming and riffing off ideas out of what you have been seeding in this thread, and I'll come back later with a more coherent &quot;updated Boston Unveiled&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Zooroos: Ugh, I *hate* it when that happens. Once my posts even begin to get moderately long, I get paranoid &amp; self-annoyed with that impending sense that the forum will eat my words.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure I\u2019m missing and/or misremembering things; but I tried to capture both my own observations and the observations of others.<br /> <br /> Also, no worries about the BU thing - I was being facetious <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It was an amusing confusion, once I pieced things together.<br /> <br /> Bonus thought: I\u2019ve always been keen on the idea that the Brotherhood\u2019s Athenaeum coincided with the <a href=\"http://www.bostonathenaeum.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Boston Athen\u00e6um</a>. YMMV, etc., etc. I just happen to like the word play.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=542422#post542422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of those points aren't kinks, they're just decisions you don't like. The Nemean being Thearch and not an Arrow for example, makes perfect sense in terms of the two order books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all of what I mentioned reflects my likes. Honestly, most of the items were mentioned because I or others found them to be <i>odd</i> choices, or at logger heads with how things in the \u2018meta-setting\u2019 began vs. how they wound up.<br /> <br /> For example, I don\u2019t particularly take issue with the Nemean\u2019s Order affiliation. (Mainly due to the motivations behind the Noose\u2019s post-Epona inception.) But it certainly seems to be a recurring point of consternation or confusion. Moreover, I do think it\u2019s worth considering alternatives to see how they play out.<br /> <br /> And yes, it\u2019s true, <u>Silver Ladder</u> did spend a chunk of text reconciling The Nemean with being a thearch, to the extent that it may have been an underlying objective for the text. Of course, the book basically informs us that his whole deal is being an \u2018anti-thearch.\u2019<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, <u>Silver Ladder\u2019</u>s sections on Initiation (or thereabouts, iirc) really makes one question just how the heck Arathnos \u201cthe Mistake\u201d got inducted into the Order. Then again, I think that the character and his circumstances are definitely fertile grounds for something more interesting, with the right tweaks (if desired). (And, of course, this level of dissection probably won\u2019t even matter to 80% of the games out there.) But hey, if Thanatos the Uncrowned King w/a death fetish can do it\u2026 :P<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t recall anything in <u>Adamantine Arrow</u> precluding someone like the Nemean as a member. If anything, in combination with various passages from <u>Sanctum &amp; Sigil,</u> the book highlights the ease with which Arrow leaders could adopt such an aspect. While they may not be *good* Arrows, it certainly can and does happen happen (and is as reasonable as anti-thearch).<br /> <br /> Of course, I haven\u2019t reviewed <u>Adamantine Arrow</u> for \u2026 over a year+. You could very well be aware of something that I\u2019m not. If so, you may not fond of how the Axe, Tiamat or Tempest being Arrows. Two of them revel/uphold/emulate the Nemean\u2019s approach and outlook while the third *could* be considered an oath breaker. (Not that we have all that much history therein; but, then again, I actually quite like that particular conflict.)<br /> <br /> Revisiting your earlier aspersion, I want to reiterate that the points I raised aren\u2019t necessarily due to a personal *dislike*. Rather, they are decisions that I don\u2019t <b>understand</b>, or that I feel demonstrate a conflict b/t how certain facets of Awakening were envisioned in 2005 (?) compared to 2012 or so. Subtle difference, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Of course, as I said, there are decisions that I don\u2019t <i>agree</i> with - For example, I think the core book would\u2019ve benefited more from having a setting that was bog standard in setup, since that example could be used to show how things \u2018are supposed to look\u2019 (in as much as the nWoD would allow). (Whether by itself or if two settings were included in the book, I just think that the fundamental goal of a core book is to illuminate the \u2018core experience\u2019; as such, when a singular example is presented, many will consider that example to be the de facto setup. Then again, I\u2019m not a psychologist who studies learning.) I also wish that the authors approached the details of the Secret Concord / Shadow Chorus in a manner akin to <u>VII</u> - Not as thoroughly, but 2-3 example options with any impacted or differing setting implications highlighted in a concentrated fashion. But, then again, I\u2019m not a layout/learning/UI expert - just someone thinking 87.5% subjectively on the matter. Plus, I can only sympathize with the authors regarding the sort of \u2018split-nature\u2019 of the book; chunks of the setting are in the core book and others are in the setting book, making it a bit hard to corral into an organized, coherent whole.<br /> <br /> So it follows that If you *do* have any resolutions or considerations to any of the points that I\u2019ve mentioned, I\u2019d love to read your thoughts. After all, I\u2019m sure there\u2019s all sorts of ways to make the pieces click - especially since there\u2019s certainly plenty of empty space to add. And even if I don\u2019t personally find them amenable, someone else might! Plus, I may learn something - or see something that I either forgot or missed.<br /> <br /> Apologies after the fact for the incoherent and ill-organized posting. Sadly, I don't have as much time to spend on my posts as I would like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/793-phil","name":"phil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T10:06:40-07:00","id":547240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes, it\u2019s true, <u>Silver Ladder</u> did spend a chunk of text reconciling The Nemean with being a thearch, to the extent that it may have been an underlying objective for the text. Of course, the book basically informs us that his whole deal is being an \u2018anti-thearch.\u2019 </div> </div> </div>I don't think it does that at all. It illustrates how thearchs end up in that situation, and how it's the basic imperatives of the organisation that drive them to it. He's not an anti-thearch, he's a thearch who has fallen into the same trap that a lot of them do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can\u2019t recall anything in <u>Adamantine Arrow</u> precluding someone like the Nemean as a member. </div> </div> </div>Their basic tenets. Yeah, he has a lot of Arrow flunkies, but that's what their philosophy tells them to be to an extent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also wish that the authors approached the details of the Secret Concord / Shadow Chorus in a manner akin to <u>VII</u> - Not as thoroughly, but 2-3 example options with any impacted or differing setting implications highlighted in a concentrated fashion. </div> </div> </div>I think you're right there. It's irritating that there seems to be a correct answer the authors had in mind, we just aren't told what it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T11:20:19-07:00","id":547357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=547240#post547240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're right there. It's irritating that there seems to be a correct answer the authors had in mind, we just aren't told what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically the &quot;canon&quot; answer to the Secret Concord is given in one of the stories of the Mage Chronical Anthology (hint: it has something to do with the rampaging cannibals Malcolm mentioned). But it never bothered me that they left it an open question. It enables the ST to make it whatever they want. But I agree some options would have been nice.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And I know the answer is late. But better a late answer than no answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T12:31:11-07:00","id":547432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Technically the &quot;canon&quot; answer to the Secret Concord is given in one of the stories of the Mage Chronical Anthology (hint: it has something to do with the rampaging cannibals Malcolm mentioned). </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I saw people referring to it, but I've only just gotten around to reading it, and I'm only only a page or two into the first Nemean story (that's actually why I decided to start reading it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it never bothered me that they left it an open question. It enables the ST to make it whatever they want. </div> </div> </div>I guess, just I'm not going to come up with as good a story as the professional writers; epseically seeing as the setting is already their creation anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T13:54:24-07:00","id":547480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=547432#post547432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess, just I'm not going to come up with as good a story as the professional writers; epseically seeing as the setting is already their creation anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>You shouldn't think that way. Those professional writers are also just gamers like you and me, and there is no reason your story would be inferior to what they think of. The main difference is possibly that they have more experience.<br /> <br /> So believe in yourself and keep trying. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:12:33-07:00","id":548780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=547480#post547480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You shouldn't think that way. Those professional writers are also just gamers like you and me, and there is no reason your story would be inferior to what they think of. The main difference is possibly that they have more experience.<br /> <br /> So believe in yourself and keep trying. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>While this is true, I think Michael's broader point still stands - and is an important one to keep in mind when developing a 'setting supplement' (regardless of system):<ul><li>The general audience for such books <i>tends</i> to be STs (GMs, etc.) (Although some players may just want to see the 'stories', etc.)</li> <li>STs (etc.) who are confident in their setting-building-fu aren't going to feel the need to purchase a setting (except to mine for ideas, save time, or to fulfill a semi-plottish interest)</li> </ul><br /> This means that the primary purchasing audiences for such a book are (typically) looking to minimize the time investment and/or have their hand held on the setting front OR are curious about things from some sort of plot perspective.<br /> <br /> The value of variation and fluidity in a pre-assembled setting is seen as a way for the ST to put their own spin on things, as well as preserving certain 'mysteries' for instances where a potential player has digested the published setting material. But, by the above standards, purchasing a setting book that says, &quot;Do it yourself&quot; for the linchpin conceits can feel like a slap in the face (or, more likely, frustration &amp; a waste of $). This is why I like the <u>VII</u> approach - it maintained the toolbox utility while providing ready-to-use inserts for the antagonists. Of course, the problem with the <u>VII</u> approach is that one only has three options to choose from. Striking a balance is probably the way to go for future endeavors.<br /> <br /> Just because someone <i>can</i> come up with something great on their own, doesn't mean they want to - or even have the time to do so.<br /> <br /> Back on the initial topic, briefly!,<ul><li>Devourers of the Flesh were a pretty bit of Boston flavor, per <u>AA</u>, iirc.</li> <li>And, if one wanted to get current-affairs-y, one might find inspiration in the House of Ariadne's use of the Boston Marathon as a celebration (<u>Legacies: Sublime</u>) and the historically recent bombing thereof.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/793-phil","name":"phil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T16:05:20-07:00","id":549476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>phil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=548780#post548780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>And, if one wanted to get current-affairs-y, one might find inspiration in the House of Ariadne's use of the Boston Marathon as a celebration (<u>Legacies: Sublime</u>) and the historically recent bombing thereof.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Incredibly surreal night. Almost no one on the streets downtown. No cars, no pedestrians, almost no sound. There was a light misting of rain, and emergency and city vehicles standing by almost silently.<br /> <br /> Then a few days later the entire city shut down as the police zeroed in on the remaining suspect. That night, a Friday, IIRC, most nightlife places were closed even after the (largely empty) trains started running again. The person I was dating at the time and I stopped into a crappy Irish-type bar for dinner because it was the only thing we could find open, and I ran into a load of people I knew from my job on the other side of the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4030-alexs","name":"AlexS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T06:15:22-07:00","id":550046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AlexS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=549476#post549476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Incredibly surreal night. Almost no one on the streets downtown. No cars, no pedestrians, almost no sound. There was a light misting of rain, and emergency and city vehicles standing by almost silently.<br /> <br /> Then a few days later the entire city shut down as the police zeroed in on the remaining suspect. That night, a Friday, IIRC, most nightlife places were closed even after the (largely empty) trains started running again. The person I was dating at the time and I stopped into a crappy Irish-type bar for dinner because it was the only thing we could find open, and I ran into a load of people I knew from my job on the other side of the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Marathon Mondays. For some reason, I remember nothing from the day - except that I'm certain the morning traffic was nonexistent. But I remember that night; well, the earliest hours of Tuesday, at least. Toiling away at some project for work or maybe school (possibly multiple projects) at &quot;I really should be asleep&quot; o'clock only to become morbidly enthralled at surreal (really, only word for it) the gunfire-in-the-streets drama that was unfolding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/793-phil","name":"phil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T07:48:18-07:00","id":550118,"title":"","content":"OK, I'm at work, so I'll toss my ideas around in no particular order:<br /> <br /> * Regarding the Devourers of the Flesh, there's a cabal of cannibal arrows in my planned chronicle. The two founding members of this cabal were senior Noose arrows that came too close to the truth about the Secret Concord and too fond of human flesh to keep it up with the witches' farce. (What happened with the other senior Noose members, asked Phil? Here's my answer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> * I'll go check both the Sublime for the Boston Marathon reference and the Ancient because I think Culsu could be a fine Thread-cutter (Her and Hydra, even implying a secret relationship between the two).<br /> <br /> * Apollonia went Vidanti after the death of Ferrum's brother ('cause they were lovers in my mind, and her being devastated and heartstruck is the only explanation I could conceive for staying behind in the order).<br /> <br /> * The Subtle Ones have operated in the Massachusetts Bay colony almost since its inception, attracted to the promised 'Shining city on the Hill' and manipulating puritan culture to better accept the sacred work they were intending for the region. However, Epona's Chariot curse on Salem and Danvers and an untimely defection of a Subtle One to the Seers of the Throne meant their ambitious plans were torn apart. The Antinomian Controversy (<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antinomian_Controversy\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antinomian_Controversy</a> ) is seen by the legacy as evidence of that failure. Nowadays the Seers Subtle Ones outnumber the original legacy. Jeremiah and now Simon belong to the original Ahl-i-batin line, but there are at least half a dozen members spread along New England, New York state and Montreal still thwarting the efforts of their wayward brothers and sisters.<br /> <br /> * Did you notice the Order leaderships are absent or seriously downplayed in the book? With the exception of Potestas with Order Status 5, no other mage have order status that high. Ferrum has Arrow status 4, Culsu has Guardian status 4, and both The Nemean and Davy Jones have Order status 3 in their respective orders. That could mean that either there is a weak leadership all around the region, or that the setting could be retconned by placing some caucus leaders to fill in the upper echelons and bring the setting in line with the 2nd edition changes. What do you people think about this?<br /> <br /> * I'm pondering about the local Seers hierarchy and the overarching Iron Pyramid of the New England Tetrarchy. I've been following the Iron Pyramid thread postings ( <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/546963-show-me-your-iron-pyramid\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...r-iron-pyramid</a>), and I think I'll go for masonic titles with a dash of neocapitalist, governmental red-tape trappings. Still a work in progress, though.<br /> <br /> * One interesting avenue of exploration, setting-wise, is the relationship between the American Independence War, the American Civil War and the birth of the Nameless orders that would eventually coalesce into the Free Council at the turn of the 20th century. In particular I'm thinking about the role the Ebon Noose covenant played in all of these, since it was a loose confederation of disenfranchised witches that rejected the Stone Assembly consilium yet didn't care much for the grander libertarians ideals of the time. It could even be possible at one time that the core Ebon Noose cabal didn't have any Diamond mages at all in their roster.<br /> <br /> * For the Mysterious Dynasty of Proximi that Numa belongs to, I'm thinking about a Spirit-worshipping cult in Ipswich tended by these Proximi, with the heritage cabal leader at the top of the cult ritually assuming the mantle of head of the spirit court (that's why Numa has the rote, BTW, he has to continue the legacy). The spirits Numa rules over are ancestor spirits and knowledge spirits of ancient Atlantis, or at least some the earlier refugee bloodlines that survived the cataclism of the Time Before. So, while he's in Ipswich he's found that the spirit wilds are behaving strange, and the Wood of Empty Houses could be a powerful lure for him that could allow him to contact more spirits from ancient Atlantis.<br /> <br /> * Khumeia's Proximus family has a long and bloody feud with the Seers of the Throne from France, particularly against the Ministry of Paternoster. I'm tempted to use this Silver Dynasty as a Dan Brown homage of occult caretakers of the royal blood of Atlantis, hoping to reinstate the &quot;Blood of the Dragon&quot; heir in her rightful throne once Hieraconis finally comes. However, I'm not yet sold on that particular idea. Besides, I'm not sure what could they be doing in Boston anyway. Any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","user":"Zooroos","date":".  misplaced word 06-11-2015, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T13:43:57-07:00","id":559742,"title":"","content":"Responding to a few of those and throwing a few of mine out there...<br /> <br /> I think Hydra makes sense as a thread-cutter. In fact I feel it would be more interesting if more mages in Boston had legacies, creating extra ties between them, going between orders and cabals. It depends a lot on what role the legacies have in the setting. I think in Dave's setting a legacy is something a &quot;mature&quot; mage is expected to join, but I dunno what the official line is.<br /> <br /> The secret conflict between Subtle Ones sounds awesome. With their attainments it makes particular sense that no one else is really aware of this. I suppose the Gray Pope would fit as the most senior member of the Seer Subtle Ones... showing how far they have fallen in their service to the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> Leadership in general is absent or downplayed in Boston Unveiled. They have one councillor less than the norm (only 4 + the nemean). It makes sense to me that Boston isn't considered that important and that some of the order members might be part of other caucuses. Silver Ladder is particularly absent, which fits with the Nemean being an embarrassment to the rest of his order. His presence is preventing himself and those close to him from gaining status within the order. Status 4 is plenty to &quot;run&quot; a caucus, I think... so Guardians, Mysterium and Arrows are actually covered. The Free Council is a bit of joke in the area, isolationalists or bloody pirates, so them not having a lot of status makes sense. I think I would go with leadership being weak in some areas, and with this being a symptom of some of Bostons issues (the Nemean's tyranny and the council's decline) and a sign of Boston not being very visible on the global scale. Also fits with the Seers having a small presence in the city and not doing anything about it for several decades. <br /> <br /> Personally I'm lazy enough that I'll simply make the Seers in Boston part of the example Iron Pyramid in the book. It is mentioned as the one covering most of North America and I kinda like weird mixture of buddhism and masonic titles. <br /> <br /> I got the impression that the Ebon Noose was more a move by the Silvar Ladder to move in and absorb a bunch of the apostate mages coming into the area... something they have been very succesful in, until now. The independence war is an interesting subject in Boston though, got some ideas there. More on that in a later post :P<br /> <br /> The Sanguine Laurel being the heart of a spirit-focused proximi and Numa leading his own court is brilliant. I like the link to the Wood of Empty Houses, it's a fitting temptation (and easy source of Very Bad Things). The relationship between Numa's court and the Austere Stone might be an interesting area as well. I could easily imagine a constant, slow-boiling conflict where the Austere Stone seeks to make Numa's court part of it, and the proximi constantly being engaged in low-level skirmishes to prevent this from happening.<br /> <br /> Regarding Khumeia and co., I'm actually planning to replace them with the Ancients from Reign of the Exarchs (which I am intending to use :P)... or perhaps meld them together. I like them as exiles from some other consillium, who were too obnoxious. They are basically Silver Ladder supremacists... or something like it. The idea of them having a cult of proximi around them that they brought with them, basically a personality cult, fits the bill as well. Their position in Boston could just be where they are gathering strength and licking their wounds, after being kicked out of another consillium. Maybe they are arming themselves for revenge? I like their proximi is a personality cult, showcasing how mages can control the lives of &quot;mortals&quot; around them if they do not impose limits on themselves. Every member of the cabal being worshipped like Gods, that sort of thing. Something that leaves a bad taste in the mouths of other mages. Might be a bit on the nose though.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Seer ministeries, which ministry to you think Psychomemetic Operations and the Asylum should belong to? Scorpio fits the bill as Pratorians. I guess Harvard would make sense as a Hegemonic stronghold, being all about controlling the ruling class. Would also indicate why the Seers aren't bringing more resources into Boston - the ministry that is supposed to care is on the decline.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2206-suicide-king","name":"Suicide King","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T14:21:59-07:00","id":559804,"title":"","content":"One thing that's more focused on in 2nd edition is that consilliums need a raison d'\u00eatre - some reason for attracting mages to form the critical mass for a consillium, other than just hanging out. Boston's is obviously the Secret Concord, but I think it lacks oomph. The Secret Concord mostly seems to determine who rules in Boston, interest in it is actively discouraged and none of the mages and cabals in Boston seem to be investigating it (except the Lodge of the Either Chambers, for obvious reasons). It is very local in nature - Boston mages care about it, but it's hard to see how it attracts and keep mages in the area.<br /> <br /> The Astral plane's special properties in Boston is a good reason to stick around there. Having a shortcut into the Astral that is easier than normal in terms of meditation and doesn't require a powerful Hallow could be a draw. <br /> <br /> One idea I've been slinging around is that something weird is going on with the Liberty Road. It is weird enough in itself, but maybe it could be a symptom of something that is happening in Boston and elsewhere that could attract interested mages. In some ways the myths and mythology around the independence war seem to be supplanting the reality of it. Maybe a weird, idealized version of the past is slowly manifesting in Boston. A lot of the wild myths about the founding fathers and the independence war is becoming reality and supplanting the truth. There is a conflict taking place, influenced by all the different groups trying to harness the myths to their purpose - the Tea Party being the most obvious culprit. It's really more of an mage: the ascenscion theme, but it could work here as a draw because it isn't supposed to be happening. Could be linked to the Wood of Empty Houses - things are slipping in there that shouldn't be, as the mythical version of the independence war and the events supplants the real history. <br /> <br /> Any idea of what a different central draw to Boston could be?<br /> <br /> Another thing I've been pondering is the different mortal secret societies that form the heart of the Seers, the Silver Ladder, the Mysterium and the Guardians mortal supporters in the area. I like the idea of them having very different flavors.<br /> I like the Seer's cults as being exemplified by the Skull and Bones Society (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skull_and_Bones\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skull_and_Bones</a>). I see them as rich socielites and coming politicians looking for an occult &quot;fix&quot;. It's not about self-improvement, it's not about getting a deeper understanding of some mystery. It's about networking, improving your material life and getting that feeling of being in the presence of something supernatural and special. I know the Skull and Bones society is in Yale, but it's easy to imagine something similar in Harvard. A bunch of cults, a guilty pleasure for young powermongers in training, a manifestation of the Hedgemonic Ministry's hold on the souls of the ruling class.<br /> <br /> The cults that are affiliated with the Diamond Orders are mainly Masonic Orders and cults. They are about self-improvement and searching for something deeper. Most of it is a dog-and-pony show, but it's still fertile ground for recruiting hangarounds for the orders. Masonic occultism, to my limited knowledge, is all about harnessing symbols to improve oneself. I haven't ironed this completely out yet, but I think one of the ways you can tell the difference between cultists who are being led around by their nose, and those who are actually being helped closer to awakening, is by whether they are adding lots of new symbols or deepening their knowledge of a handful. Those who are focusing on mastering a few symbols, understanding the allagories completely, are actually being drawn toward a path. Those just collecting them like trading cards are focused on the rituals and the prestige of it, being drawn toward the smoke and mirrors, rather than the deeper truths. This difference is a remnant of the Guardians' labyrinth, something the Shadow Chorus is in the process of bringing under their purview once again.<br /> <br /> The gist: The Seers' cults are about getting a &quot;fix&quot; of the occult, strange and supernatural. THe Diamond's are about self-improvement in some form, as exemplified by the freemasons. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2206-suicide-king","name":"Suicide King","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T16:34:10-07:00","id":559962,"title":"","content":"A central draw to Boston? There is an entire section of town that functions like one big demesne, that I think would draw the interest of everybody including the Seers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T15:32:52-07:00","id":562277,"title":"","content":"Good point, the Combat Zone is pretty much dismissed in the book as not being of much interest and of being fading, but that never sat right with me. Especially with the new rules, an area with no paradox means you can work some huge spell effects and rituals without risk. I can easily imagine that being the Cabal to control it would be a huge conflict... actually I think it might be important enough that there likely is a consillium decision saying that no single Cabal can control it, that one must allow others to access it. Neat little conflict there.<br /> <br /> So, just to sum up.<br /> Reasons to go to Boston, and to stay there:<br /> The Combat Zone<br /> A huge, unspecified demesne. It seems there should be soul stones there, but they can't be found. It's plagued by a &quot;cabal&quot; of Banishers who occasionally attack mages trying to use the demesne.<br /> <br /> The Bleached Schooner<br /> A way to enter the astral, without needing a powerful hallow and with easier requirements for meditation can be a powerful draw. Mages interested in the Astral come to Boston for this. A small idea is that there is actually a belief going around that the quality and type of poem recited can have an effect on the journey, so a few poets make a bit of cash selling poems to mages.<br /> <br /> The Secret Concord<br /> Mostly of interest to local mages, but still, it is mysterious and possibly connected to big things. That interest in it is actively discouraged by the Nemean, the Ebon Noose and the White Putnams doesn't prevent mages from coming and asking questions. The risk of being flayed alive by mysterious forces just adds spice to it.<br /> <br /> The Wood of Empty Houses<br /> While the same, or similar, phenomenon is found all over the world (particular in places where a native population has been displaced or been wiped out), the Empty houses are most common in and around Massachusetts. The leap from forgotten mundane concepts to forgotten supernal concepts isn't that big, so mages looking for lost rotes or atlantean lore visit them... as well as free councillers looking for lost human crafts. Hell, some mages are historians and interested just because.<br /> <br /> Treasure hunting<br /> The Stone Assembly, the original Emerald Scroll, several Seer Pylons, have all been wiped out in and around Boston. Some of them very quickly and abruptly. Though presumably most of their treasures have been found or secured by their orders now, there are always stories and rumors. A few mages come to Boston looking for the treasures of the past.<br /> <br /> Peace, Quiet and Community<br /> I think for some mages Boston has the right mixture of a community, but also lots of room to be left alone. Those mages who want to pursue their own thing, without interference from others, but yet also have other mages to meet and exchange ideas/favors/etc with, probably like Boston. There is a lot of room to &quot;opt out&quot; of the awakened community, but also other mages to talk to. Most of the Free Council in the area epitomize this - they don't bother with politics at all, but still stick around.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's... 6 fairly good reason. Enough to expliain why ~100 mages stick around in Boston, other than growing up there, being apprenticed there or just ending up there through the vagaries of fate and awakened life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2206-suicide-king","name":"Suicide King","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T13:39:44-07:00","id":1112318,"title":"","content":"How useful is Boston Unveiled to someone running 2e who is not familiar with all the backstory and metaplot of Boston and the Nemean? I'm considering picking it up, if only for all of the premade cabals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6700-michael-tree","name":"Michael Tree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T13:45:58-07:00","id":1112322,"title":"","content":"The fiction isn't really necessary, they're just a way the setting could bear out. It's okay, I think. You won't have that much in the way of interesting or powerful stuff just going by the cabals alone, but you can always alter them around. I think the cabals tended to be order or path aligned, which can be limiting. You still have a bunch of write-ups for people and organizations, what they're like as mages and so forth, that's always good to mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T10:12:37-07:00","id":1112767,"title":"","content":"I personally think it's a great setting and very well-written, but it lacks some context for some of the cabals and political dynamics in the Consilium.<br /> <br /> My personal highlights for the setting are:<br /> <br /> - The Consilium is Cabal-aligned, instead of Path- or Order-aligned. Each have some strong themes going on.<br /> <br /> - The Nemean is a textbook-failed-state thearch begging to be deposed. He's a bully with little interest in diplomacy and legalese, but otherwise he's pretty hands off regarding individual mages' freedoms.<br /> <br /> - The Secret Concord is the Big Obvious Mystery, but very little is discussed regarding how does it actually affect Consilium laws. <br /> <br /> - The Prince of 10000 Leaves is the best thing in the book, the lovecraftian horror ready to be used in your chronicle.<br /> <br /> <br /> For a 2nd Edition game, I'd take the following into account:<br /> - Is the Nemean still in charge? If not, what happens with the balance of power in the region?<br /> - What are the main Legacies influencing the area? Where are the Order Caucuses located, and how they influence the Boston &amp; Salem Consilium?<br /> - For a regional sourcebook you might want to add some extra cabals, especially since most important characters have only Order status 2-3. Guardians of the Veil, in particular, are in sore need of more sympathetic members. The Free Council could use a few more members.<br /> <br /> That's my two cents, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T15:27:17-07:00","id":1114779,"title":"","content":"I am cribbing a bunch of the characters and cabals for my London game, its a really nice resource if you want some interesting folks to drop into your own setting, as well as being a great setting by itself. <br /> <br /> My one criticism of the setting as a whole is that I would be kind of at a loss if I had someone turn up wanting to play a Guardian. The Shadow Chorus are a funky crew of oddballs, but as the settings only Canon guardians it leaves a prospective Guardian PC with very little 'order' to interact with. I am stealing them for my game, but they will be acting as a particularly shadowy part of a larger organisation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T15:37:25-07:00","id":1114787,"title":"","content":"I stole the red word cult and the prince of 100,000 leaves but ported them my city setting of New York and also used alot of the named characters/cabals to flesh out my npc's. I tried to do something with the secret concord but lack of info or interest from my players meant i didnt nail down what it was (not would i want to its a head ache). I wanted to use some of the astral things like the ship and stuff, but again my players didnt hang about and explore the astral as much as i thought they would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T03:49:19-07:00","id":1115010,"title":"","content":"I will just point to my/our started project of updating <b>Boston: Unveiled</b> as whole to 2E <b>Mage</b> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=826830#post826830\">here it starts</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T18:19:27-07:00","id":1126131,"title":"","content":"Here's a link to the Actual Play of my Boston Unveiled game: <a href=\"http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal.com/posts?order_by=oldest&amp;page=1\" target=\"_blank\">http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal....=oldest&amp;page=1</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T20:44:26-07:00","id":1126154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1126131#post1126131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a link to the Actual Play of my Boston Unveiled game: <a href=\"http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal.com/posts?order_by=oldest&amp;page=1\" target=\"_blank\">http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal....=oldest&amp;page=1</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Cool! What about Arachne's ghost familiar? I get she managed to manipulate another mage into binding it to her, but why would she go with a ghost? I've had a bunch of ghost familiars in my game so I'm curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T01:25:55-07:00","id":1126219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1126131#post1126131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a link to the Actual Play of my Boston Unveiled game: <a href=\"http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal.com/posts?order_by=oldest&amp;page=1\" target=\"_blank\">http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal....=oldest&amp;page=1</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This 1e?. Asking because im reading through the old quickstart and demo and seeing how much conversion to 2e it needs before i try running it for a new group.<br /> <br /> <i>*edit never mind checked the dates posted and it has to be 1st ed?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 08-09-2017, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T05:27:26-07:00","id":1127579,"title":"","content":"Yeah. It's 1e. Arachne's ghost familiar was mainly for character reasons (her Grandmother's ghost).<br /> <br /> I think that Gloria Mundi would mostly work as written. You'd probably have to adjust Bans and Banes for some of the Spirits, but otherwise it would work I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T05:01:20-08:00","id":1361255,"title":"","content":"<br /> I just started running a Boston Chronicle for 3 players of 3 Mage the Awakening 2e characters.<br /> <br /> 2 of the players never played wod or cod games. One played Requiem 2nd with me as ST. I myself never ever played Mage before only Requiem and Masquerade and some Masquerade LARP. We are a colorfull group of Fathers living here in Germany.<br /> <br /> I needed a Mage Beginners Chronicle. Couldn't find one in public domain and couldn't find one on drivethu. So I decided to &quot;design&quot; a Mage version of the New Orleans Chronic and the Danse de la Morte story.<br /> <br /> Cast and City<br /> The BU Dilivered me the Mage Cast, but I have changed some places. Like I changed the Manray(Neutral ground club) and made it the Middle East/Zuzu &amp;c. So I refitted all places so they have real world representation and marked them on Googlemaps/Googleearth . As it's a bit difficult to transport the look and feel of a place that is on the other side of the world by storytelling only, I use tools like Google streetview and Zillow(for intiriors).<br /> (Did you know that there are NO walled estates anywhere in Boston....while all Sanctums are located in walled estates in the BU book?)<br /> I will add the Vampire Cast from Chicago and I will also add the God Machines Angels to help out on the side of the Seers, as surprise.<br /> <br /> Introductory Idea for the Characters<br /> To make the whole story evolve around the players I took inspiration from the Buffalo Chronicle that is flashed out in the Mage Chroncilers Guide.<br /> January 15, 1919 was the Boston Molassacre several cityblocks were hit by a 7 m high tsunamy of hot molasses 23 died 160 injured...<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Molasses_Flood\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/BostonMolassesDisaster.jpg/1280px-BostonMolassesDisaster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Molasses_Flood\" target=\"_blank\"> Great Molasses Flood - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Molasses_Flood\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Molasses_Flood </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was the result of an attack of a Seer on a gathering of a group of Pentacle Mages and he wanted to make their end to be sure. In my book The Boston police strike was a retaliation of the Pentacle Mage against the Seers influence.<br /> The Molassacre had a paradox effect: &quot;Boston will sleep for a 100 years.&quot;<br /> And no mage awakened the next 100 years in Boston...all mages in the area came from elsewhere or awakened elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Play so far<br /> First day of play was the January 15, 2019 ^^ , We played the awakening of each player. Starting with the news on the radion about the jubelee of the molassacre and the laying down of a plate with the names of the victims at the childrens league baseball diamant Langone Park.<br /> So uppon waking up the characters entered the Awakening...<br /> When they got back into the fallen world each player was standing at on e of the bases looking toward each other, But they were not in January/2019 anymore but in December/2019.<br /> <br /> Play planned<br /> So before entering the real story they can deal with small problems like Family, IRS, How to get registered a live again...I intend to nake all the paperwork to get easier by dealing with the Vampire cast that controlls the courts and Administration.<br /> Like in danse Macarbre I will send an emergency mentor , it will be the MIT professor of the Benefit cabal.<br /> This guy will help them to find proper mentors that show them how rotes and improviosed spells and healing and mana and shadownames work. Also they will tell about the orders and the local powerstructure and the Seers.<br /> <br /> Confusion<br /> I have still no idea how to deal with the secret concord. I hope it will resolve it self...If the players speculate once they get that it exists I will pick something they come up with. They will never know...and will think that they are soo smart knowing it right away.<br /> <br /> <br /> Protagonists<br /> <br /> A Houngan (Moros)<br /> Living in Roxbury<br /> Having a Vodou and ocult shop<br /> <br /> Rich Kid, Hacktivist and Student (Acanthus)<br /> beeing an Orphant he inherited all his parents wealth (Basically little bruce wayne...but not that rich)<br /> (this player only had character Ideas that were bad, like FSB Killer covering as a regular student &amp;c.)<br /> <br /> Egyption Sufi Mystic (Obrimos)<br /> Studies at Medical school<br /> Working as driver and carpark manager for Rich Kid<br /> <br /> <br /> As I'm a beginner I don't think it will help a lot of people, but here is how I transfered BU to become usefull to 2nd edition Mage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25682-quickanddirty","user":"QuickAndDirty","date":". 01-16-2020, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25682-quickanddirty","name":"QuickAndDirty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T06:38:50-08:00","id":1361265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Did you know that there are NO walled estates anywhere in Boston....while all Sanctums are located in walled estates in the BU book?) </div> </div> </div>I've noticed that, the book was clearly written before easily accessed aerial maps. You see it in the demo too.<br /> <br /> To be fair though, only two are actually in Boston itself that I remember.<br /> <br /> I gave the Putnams the Church Court building on Beacon St. It's a burned down church that got refitted for condos. It looks cool, and it seems the closest you'll get to having a walled green.<br /> <br /> The Academy I just moved to the Athenaeum and had the Order of the Gryphon work out of a mausoleum in the cemetery directly behind it. That has the downside of being a bit of a tourist spot, but I just said that sleepers didn't notice it for some reason... Honestly that worked pretty well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T07:34:51-08:00","id":1361273,"title":"","content":"Wow necromancy. Shoulda just made a new thread?<br /> <br /> On the topic of the secret concord, I never did get my head round it and my players didn't care so it was quickly forgotten. Don't hold your breath if you want to know for sure what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-16-2020, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T08:04:34-08:00","id":1361278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1361265#post1361265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've noticed that, the book was clearly written before easily accessed aerial maps. You see it in the demo too.<br /> <br /> To be fair though, only two are actually in Boston itself that I remember.<br /> <br /> I gave the Putnams the Church Court building on Beacon St. It's a burned down church that got refitted for condos. It looks cool, and it seems the closest you'll get to having a walled green.</div> </div> </div> </div>I chose 398 Beacon St. for the Putnams.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://goo.gl/maps/ztq84o2dtxygbzyX9\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://maps.google.com/maps/api/staticmap?center=42.3522134%2C-71.0859815&amp;zoom=19&amp;size=900x900&amp;language=en&amp;sensor=false&amp;key=AIzaSyBoYjeRtfVI0Jd8Q_9mnflo9i4sOYpShB0&amp;signature=6Bd1NK6956wWSS9MuyCEfVM-UBU\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://goo.gl/maps/ztq84o2dtxygbzyX9\" target=\"_blank\"> Google Maps </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://goo.gl/maps/ztq84o2dtxygbzyX9\" target=\"_blank\"> https://goo.gl/maps/ztq84o2dtxygbzyX9 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Find local businesses, view maps and get driving directions in Google Maps. </div> </div> </div><br /> I just couldn't find something in that region that wasn't a small house.sharing walls with other houses...<br /> Where exactly is the Church you meantioned?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1361265#post1361265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Academy I just moved to the Athenaeum and had the Order of the Gryphon work out of a mausoleum in the cemetery directly behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I put both into &quot;Bowdoin School Apartmens&quot; as it noted in the discription that they have a Cover operation going on as an elite school.<br /> And as there are no real Mannors in Boston there is not much to choose from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1361265#post1361265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That has the downside of being a bit of a tourist spot, but I just said that sleepers didn't notice it for some reason... Honestly that worked pretty well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only place I'm realy proud to have found that fit's the dsicription is the Fortress(SMG)<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://goo.gl/maps/AF7uy8A8qTixXeZv7\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://maps.google.com/maps/api/staticmap?center=42.3572512%2C-71.0942833&amp;zoom=19&amp;size=900x900&amp;language=en&amp;sensor=false&amp;key=AIzaSyBoYjeRtfVI0Jd8Q_9mnflo9i4sOYpShB0&amp;signature=CHpOKBE_0mAZyeQt-68qaUr0198\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://goo.gl/maps/AF7uy8A8qTixXeZv7\" target=\"_blank\"> Google Maps </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://goo.gl/maps/AF7uy8A8qTixXeZv7\" target=\"_blank\"> https://goo.gl/maps/AF7uy8A8qTixXeZv7 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Find local businesses, view maps and get driving directions in Google Maps. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25682-quickanddirty","user":"QuickAndDirty","date":". 01-16-2020, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25682-quickanddirty","name":"QuickAndDirty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T08:27:26-08:00","id":1361281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1361273#post1361273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow necromancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thread wasn't dead, he was just having a long slumber. just like Rosebud.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1361273#post1361273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shoulda just made a new thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, why duplicate the topic?<br /> Give me a 2nd edition Version of a mage chronicle with a plot that allows to have an entire group of characters awaken at the same time and I will write in a threat about that resource.<br /> There need to be way more beginner friendly ready to play city books. Who cares about the gimicks? It's about cool scenarios. More scenarios would be realy important to grow the player base.<br /> They should all be realy cross over friendly!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1361273#post1361273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of the secret concord, I never did get my head round it and my players didn't care so it was quickly forgotten. Don't hold your breath if you want to know for sure what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The word &quot;Konkordat&quot; allready carries a historic weight with it. If I ever name this conspiracy or treaty &quot;Geheimkonkordat&quot; the players will want to know whats behind it. Also it's nature looks like to be realy similar to the Reichskonkordat just with a secret party...<br /> If I don't want to have this road pursued, I would have to make up something else...<br /> I think the best thing would be to have the Noose and the Putnams beeing on the edge allready, just short of breaking up and neutralizing both their powers in open conflict as a result. Also this way I could give the Seers and the Angels more spotlight.<br /> <br /> I will add a Tong lead by a Scellesti for chinatown. In order to present the Chinese Banishers and the PC an oportunity to cooperate and overcome the differences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25682-quickanddirty","user":"QuickAndDirty","date":". 01-16-2020, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25682-quickanddirty","name":"QuickAndDirty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T09:33:05-08:00","id":1361287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QuickAndDirty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1361278#post1361278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where exactly is the Church you meantioned?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's on the corner of Massachusetts Avenue and Beacon St.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I put both into &quot;Bowdoin School Apartmens&quot; as it noted in the discription that they have a Cover operation going on as an elite school.<br /> And as there are no real Mannors in Boston there is not much to choose from. </div> </div> </div>That's pretty reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only place I'm realy proud to have found that fit's the dsicription is the Fortress(SMG) </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's great. Wish I hadn't already established it as a few blocks inland of the river.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T06:00:27-08:00","id":1362383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1361287#post1361287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's on the corner of Massachusetts Avenue and Beacon St.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I took that suggestion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Thanx<br /> <br /> Also under what Arcana's purview do the following criters or objects fall?<br /> -sleeping Vampire(death? matter? or both?)<br /> -walking Vampire(death? matter? life? or all 3?)<br /> -blush of life Vampire(death? matter? life? or both?)<br /> <br /> -a warm body (death? matter? life?)<br /> -a cold body (death? matter? life?)<br /> -a Schnitzel (death? matter? life?)<br /> -a blood in a bloodbag (death? matter? life?)<br /> <br /> -a Strix(spirit? death? life? or all 3?)<br /> -a Werewolf(spirit? life? or both?)<br /> -Demon/Angel (Prime? Spirit? Life? Mind?)<br /> -Demonenblooded (Life? or more?)<br /> <br /> I need to know that as I intend to have them appeat in the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25682-quickanddirty","user":"QuickAndDirty","date":". 01-21-2020, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25682-quickanddirty","name":"QuickAndDirty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T09:29:06-08:00","id":1362424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QuickAndDirty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1362383#post1362383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I took that suggestion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Thanx<br /> <br /> Also under what Arcana's purview do the following criters or objects fall?<br /> -sleeping Vampire(death? matter? or both?)<br /> -walking Vampire(death? matter? life? or all 3?)<br /> -blush of life Vampire(death? matter? life? or both?)<br /> <br /> -a warm body (death? matter? life?)<br /> -a cold body (death? matter? life?)<br /> -a Schnitzel (death? matter? life?)<br /> -a blood in a bloodbag (death? matter? life?)<br /> <br /> -a Strix(spirit? death? life? or all 3?)<br /> -a Werewolf(spirit? life? or both?)<br /> -Demon/Angel (Prime? Spirit? Life? Mind?)<br /> -Demonenblooded (Life? or more?)<br /> <br /> I need to know that as I intend to have them appeat in the chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires fall under Death in general, though their specific template powers, Disciplines and other stuff might not. Typically, to figure out what something falls under you look at its end result. A vampire is a walking talking corpse, and while other arcana might be able to do something with those, Death will be the main go to.<br /> <br /> A corpse in general will be Death, it\u2019s a dead thing.<br /> <br /> A schnitzel funnily enough could be Life, because food falls under the purview of Life.<br /> <br /> Blood is probably also going to be Life unless it\u2019s useless for living things. The Tamers of Blood are a Space/Life legacy for example.<br /> <br /> Strix are probably Death oriented.<br /> <br /> Werewolves have been officially said to be Spirit and Life.<br /> <br /> Angels and Demons are Prime and Fate.<br /> <br /> Not sure on demon blooded, but they\u2019re probably just Life, while their powers probably fall under Prime and Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T10:05:46-08:00","id":1362439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QuickAndDirty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1362383#post1362383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also under what Arcana's purview do the following criters or objects fall?</div> </div> </div> </div>Things generally doesn't fall neatly under specific Arcana. Mind can affect most of those examples because they are thinking beings. Forces can technically affect all of them by changing their temperatures.<br /> As Mrmdubois says, you've gotta look to the specific effects in order to figure out what Arcana are relevant.<br /> <br /> Manipulating the body of a vampire is generally Death because they are dead. A vampire who uses Blush of Life doesn't stop being dead so still generally Death, but messing with the biological functions that Blush of Life has activated would be Life, because biological functions fall under Life.<br /> Strix are shadows with a connection to death so definitely Death to affect them physically.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are human/spirit hybrids (extremely gross simplification), but the question is to what degree that is so. Going according to the sidebar for Mage Sight, werewolves are partially spirits on a physical level so affecting their bodies should require Life+Spirit. (Whether it be equal parts Life and Spirit, or if it's enough to just include Spirit at one or two dots, is up to the ST to decide.) Interfering with their powers, however, is just Spirit.<br /> <br /> Mages can use Fate+Prime to interact with the God-Machine (i.e. Infrastructure on a metaphysical level) and in extension probably also angels similar to how Spirit deals with spirits or Death deals with ghosts. Demons, on the other hand, are transformed into a new form and should require Life and/or Matter (depending on their physical makeup and whether they're in a Cover or not) to affect physically. I would personally forgo Fate and Prime unless you're casting a spell that interacts with a part of the demon template that would be governed by them. For example, Fate would be able to change or possibly even break a Pact that the demon hadn't cashed in.<br /> <br /> Just remember that direct template modification is beyond the scope of normal magic. You can always interfere with the results of another supernatural's powers (provided you win the Clash of Wills roll), but you can't outright remove or change how they work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-21-2020, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T14:55:08-08:00","id":1362526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1362424#post1362424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A schnitzel funnily enough could be Life, because food falls under the purview of Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>But a Schnitzel is a part of a dead body isn't it?<br /> Thanx<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25682-quickanddirty","name":"QuickAndDirty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T15:19:44-08:00","id":1362532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QuickAndDirty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1362526#post1362526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But a Schnitzel is a part of a dead body isn't it?<br /> Thanx</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as it's uncooked you could probably also cast Death spells on the part of it that's just dead meat, provided the spell does something to dead meat.<br /> <br /> Again, I want to emphasise that nothing falls neatly under a single Arcanum. That Schnitzel can be affected by certain spells from all ten Arcana. It really depends on what you want to do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T17:03:55-08:00","id":1362547,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this was asked but, what books does the Nemean show up in in meaningful fashion so I can catch up on this character? Im very sorry for asking but I dont have much time or resources to solve this myself so itd be a biiig help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T17:15:23-08:00","id":1362552,"title":"","content":"Everything about Boston, including Nemean, are in the appendix of first edition core or in Boston Unveiled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T17:24:09-08:00","id":1362554,"title":"","content":"I used Boston Unveiled mostly for it's history. My game is set there in the 1920s, a few years after the destruction of the Stone Assembly. With the war between the Emerald Scroll and Libertines as a back drop. The players Cabal is trying to find the Stone Assembly's Atheneum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T17:44:14-08:00","id":1362555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1362547#post1362547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this was asked but, what books does the Nemean show up in in meaningful fashion so I can catch up on this character? Im very sorry for asking but I dont have much time or resources to solve this myself so itd be a biiig help!</div> </div> </div> </div>Boston Unveiled, and then the timeline essentially runs &quot;Prologue: Censorious&quot; (opening fiction of The Mysterium), &quot;The Cage is the Lion's Heart&quot; (opening fiction of Silver Ladder), &quot;The Veil, Nothing More&quot; (opening fiction of Left-Hand Path), culminating in &quot;The Unmurdered Man&quot; in the Fallen World Fiction Anthology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T15:20:28-08:00","id":1362967,"title":"","content":"So who do you think was the third signatory of the Secret Compact? My guess is the Seers and the Compact was a collaboration to take down the Stone Assembly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T20:30:25-08:00","id":1362999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1362967#post1362967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So who do you think was the third signatory of the Secret Compact? My guess is the Seers and the Compact was a collaboration to take down the Stone Assembly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve always figured it was the Prince of 1,000 Leaves. Iirc, the Compact was originally formed because the settlers set off a chain of events which led to massive wendigo problems. The Compact allowed them to alter the timeline so that didn\u2019t happen. I assume what the Prince got out of the deal is that the other signatories will take no direct action to prevent the pages necessary to summon it from being assembled. Presumably, though some of the signatories have changed over time, they refuse to renege on the deal because that would mean altering the timeline further via snapback, and/or having to deal with a massive wendigo problem themselves.<br /> <br /> I also wouldn\u2019t put it past the original signatories to have asked for more than just removing the wendigo problem. They probably also got the Stone Assembly snuffed into the bargain. They were in for a penny after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-23-2020, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T20:43:25-08:00","id":1363001,"title":"","content":"Oh, man. I totally missed that connection. I have some rereading to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T05:39:00-08:00","id":1363060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1362999#post1362999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iirc, the Compact was originally formed because the settlers set off a chain of events which led to massive wendigo problems. The Compact allowed them to alter the timeline so that didn\u2019t happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>The conflict involving the wendigo is what brings the Prince into the world in the first place. The Secret Concord is created three hundred years later. The connection is that the Concord is drawn up at Salem, which is built on the location where the Noose had their original Sanctum, and where the influence of the Prince touched down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T08:20:44-08:00","id":1363081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1363060#post1363060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The conflict involving the wendigo is what brings the Prince into the world in the first place. The Secret Concord is created three hundred years later. The connection is that the Concord is drawn up at Salem, which is built on the location where the Noose had their original Sanctum, and where the influence of the Prince touched down.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yup, the concord is between the Putnums and the Noose, they signed it instead of going to war with each other over Salem. Which leads me to believe both must have found something worse for them to pause and sign it right? Its stated as a mystical pact so there has to be bad repercussions for either (and the third signatory) if it breaks right? The whole Concord thing with no explanation really does annoy me, I would rather have even a sidebar of &quot;Here is what the default Concord is&quot; and let me ignore it than tease it but never explain it.<br /> <br /> I've said before that my players didnt give a toss about the concord so luckily i didnt have to come up with wtf it was.<br /> <br /> Isnt the Nemean an abyssal entity changeling (little c) imposter from the princes reality too? Maybe that has something to do with the Concord?<br /> <br /> I did use the Ghuls from one of the blue books (i cant remember which) as similar imposters. The red word's ritual either made everybody forget that the person who was eaten existed OR if they had a doppleganger alive in the Princes reality it appeared instead and being a Ghul (cannibal) they became well respected etc. Once the Red Word realised this, they made a concerted effort to kidnap and replace people in power with Ghul imposters..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-24-2020, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T10:16:25-08:00","id":1363110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1363081#post1363081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yup, the concord is between the Putnums and the Noose, they signed it instead of going to war with each other over Salem. Which leads me to believe both must have found something worse for them to pause and sign it right? Its stated as a mystical pact so there has to be bad repercussions for either (and the third signatory) if it breaks right? The whole Concord thing with no explanation really does annoy me, I would rather have even a sidebar of &amp;quot;Here is what the default Concord is&amp;quot; and let me ignore it than tease it but never explain it.<br /> <br /> I've said before that my players didnt give a toss about the concord so luckily i didnt have to come up with wtf it was.<br /> <br /> Isnt the Nemean an abyssal entity changeling (little c) imposter from the princes reality too? Maybe that has something to do with the Concord?<br /> <br /> I did use the Ghuls from one of the blue books (i cant remember which) as similar imposters. The red word's ritual either made everybody forget that the person who was eaten existed OR if they had a doppleganger alive in the Princes reality it appeared instead and being a Ghul (cannibal) they became well respected etc. Once the Red Word realised this, they made a concerted effort to kidnap and replace people in power with Ghul imposters..</div> </div> </div> </div>Is he? I'd doesn't mention it in his entry in the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T10:50:30-08:00","id":1363122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1363110#post1363110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is he? I'd doesn't mention it in his entry in the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't. It's in the story 'The Unmurdered Man' from the Anthology. (I think.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T10:56:55-08:00","id":1363125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=1363110#post1363110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is he? I'd doesn't mention it in his entry in the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Followup from the Unmurdered Man again. He talks to Xaphan/Khonsu in the world of the Prince; I forgot the last part of the Nemean's timeline was a separate piece in the Anthology \u2014 the two-page &quot;The Human Heart&quot; covers a conversation between him and the Old Man of the Abyss.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I cultivated the Consilium\u2019s hate. I wanted them to manage themselves and stay away while I studied the Concord, my Mystery. I crossed the Threshold just before they deposed me, as I had planned. But they imprisoned me in my own mind, before I could reexamine the Concord with a more enlightened eye. I took years to remember who I really was: a Seeker whose Golden Road opens any prison. It was a slender, shimmering thing, this soul-path of mine, yet to be fully formed: a tether to the sky anchored too lightly.<br /> <br /> Its weighty replacement bleeds in my right hand.<br /> <br /> A withered man with my face still babbles under their care. I created a different body and returned to the page containing my Mystery.<br /> <br /> It was perfectly legible. The Secret Concord relied on an emissary: a noble of the 100,000 Leaves, a shaman to keep the worlds apart, and give each one its necessary sacrifices.<br /> <br /> In that moment, I remembered feeding the \u2018wolves\u2019 of my youth.<br /> <br /> \u201cBaron Maahes, have you awakened from your dream to come home?\u201d The Old Man rocks forward on his cane, extending a hand. I ignore it and open the door to his hut myself. I whisper syllables that have never been heard in this universe. I have a spell to complete. But first:<br /> <br /> \u201cWas I always the Baron? Or did I make myself the Prince\u2019s when I approached the Threshold?\u201d<br /> <br /> The Old Man shrugs and smirks. \u201cYou gave that Mystery the only answer you knew.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat doesn\u2019t answer my question.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou didn\u2019t answer mine just now, Baron, but I can see what it will be.\u201d </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T10:58:37-08:00","id":1363127,"title":"","content":"Thanks for reminding me what actually went down.<br /> <br /> I agree that the Concord is a bit lackluster. It's supposed to be the central Mystery of Boston, buuuut how do other Mages get all their magical hoodoo up in it? The strict policy of the Noose and the Putnams is to lock everyone else out of getting any information about it at all.<br /> <br /> What are the obvious benefits of the Concord? It seems that being a signatory ensures that your cabal will continue in perpetuity at the reins of power in Boston. Ok, cool...I guess. This is really only beneficial if your players want to be in power. I can think of reasons why that would be the case, you get access to all the other stuff going on in Boston, you probably don't have to worry about the Seers in the universities taking you out, it gives you a platform from which to start shaping the rest of the mystical world because you can be assured your legacy (mundane kind) will last. Most of the time Boston is kind of live and let live though, so as long as you're willing to dodge the Seers, the occasional Tremere, and play nice with your neighbors Boston is pretty open to you to do whatever you want. So you can safely ignore the Concord if you're interested in literally anything else.<br /> <br /> So, how do you make the Concord more engaging? The first thing that comes to mind is that it -must- be used to interfere with your pcs. Seems to happen a lot in Boston anyway, the Nemean has the Mysterium, or at least Khonsu, at his beck and call whether they like it or not. It's probably safe to assume that whoever is a signatory to the Concords basically gets to boss other Mages around in a way that's almost unconscionable in other settings because of how Mage society is generally organized with student/mentor/cabal relationships and the Consilium usually only existing for conflict resolution. The Concord seems to empower its signatories to use the Consilium for more than conflict resolution, making it more like a really, really loose dictatorship. That may have just been the Nemean though since his goal was to basically establish a dictatorship in order to prove how shit Boston was in order to force him to be deposed and cause reform.<br /> <br /> That got a bit rambly, tldr, have the signatories of the Concord interfere with your pcs so that they take an interest in it either to make the interference stop, and/or so they can seize the reins of power.<br /> <br /> Whatever or whoever the third signatory is can be one of the things interfering with your pcs as well. The third signatory is certainly a Mystery unto themselves. Though as presented seems less approachable to me than trying to go through the other two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T12:01:59-08:00","id":1363157,"title":"","content":"That spurs me to reread &quot;The unmurdered Man&quot; and &quot;The human heart&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-24-2020, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T14:42:42-08:00","id":1363198,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">So here is my rambling attempt to flesh this plot out in a way that actually engages the PCs.</span> I haven't actually read the Numean short stories so this may contradict that or some of the other stuff in the books. Retcon happens.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">In 1906 the Ebon Noose and White Putnams went to war over Salem, both with intention of claiming the ground and lifting the perceived curse.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Instead they discovered the curse was the Prince of 100,00 Leaves, an Abyssal entity that is trying to re-format history into its own image. They realized they were not strong enough to defeat this entity. So they struck a bargain with it. </span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">The Compact: The Ebon Noose and the White Putnams agreed to perform oblations in honor of the Prince that would satiate the being, in exchange they get to destroy any new Leaves that appear in our reality and they get the support of the Red Word (to an extent). Creating a truce that maintains the status quo of reality.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">The oblations they have to perform? Providing awakened mages to feed to the Prince at the </span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Temple of Holy Devouring.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">So now the Ebon Noose has to start a trafficking operation and to make this happen has to take control of the Concilium. So they enlist some unlikely allies to further their plans: The Seers and the Tremere.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">The Seers have a recruiting operation that rivals the Emerald Scrolls. The Noose makes a pact with them, &quot;we won't interfere with your operations if you send a couple of newly awakened mages to us each year&quot; The Seers agree in exchange for help getting rid of the Stone Assembly, whose sanctum is on the Seers' backdoor step.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">The Seers take down the Stone Assembly and their allies with the secret help of the Noose and Putnams.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">They also sponsor and set up a group of Libertines that they use to coopt the Emerald Scrolls Labrynth.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Now they are getting 2 to 5 newly awakened sent to them each year through their trafficking operation. But they can't sacrifice any awakened mage to the Prince, it has to be someone who wants to be sacrificed, someone who begs for it.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">The Noose who control Danvers, make a pact with the Tremere. They set them up in the Danvers Asylum. The kidnapped Initiates are sent to the asylum. The Tremere get to keep one for themselves each year and the rest they torture, gaslight and manipulate until their psyche breaks and they think it is in their best interest to die.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Once broken the Sacrifice is sent to Howard's Rock, where they are laid on the alter in the </span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Temple of Holy Devouring, where the victim is eaten alive by the Red Word. This rite is performed twice a year.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">By 1935, the Stone Assembly, the Emerald Scroll and most of their allies are destroyed or defunct. The Concilium is gone and the Ebon Noose can operate with impunity. Everything works without a hitch for about 50 years.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">By the 1980s and 90s things start to fall apart. The Nemean comes to power, but he is interested in finding a way to coopt or change the Compact or securing a future for himself with the Prince of 100,000 Leaves. The Tremere of the Asylum fracture and disband, requiring the Noose or the Putnams to &quot;break&quot; the Sacrifices themselves.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">By the present day, the trafficking operation has become so ineffective that they are in danger of not being able to fulfill the terms of the compact. The Seers are their only steady source of Sacrifices now, but they have figured out what the Sacrifices are for and have increased their demands in exchange for their services. The Seers don't believe the Exarchs would ever let the Prince succeed so they don't fear endangering the Compact.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">The Red Word, who have gotten so used to this arrangement, they want to see it continue at any cost. They get desperate and start to recruit Sacrifices themselves by targeting new cabals or kidnapping young members of older cabals.</span></span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","user":"Jeremysbrain","date":". 01-24-2020, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T16:25:21-08:00","id":1363219,"title":"","content":"Another consideration. If one of the players generate a Fragment from a Time paradox, the Ebon Noose and White Putnams will know about it and will come to take it and either kill the mage or wipe his memory. It's also possible the Red Word might find out about it and try to retrieve it themselves so they can hide it from the Noose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T17:22:39-08:00","id":1363224,"title":"","content":"Now I wonder, under 2ed rules, should Howard`s Rock count as an Abyssal Emenation? Should the Red Word be a Proximi cult? Abyssal Proximi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","user":"Jeremysbrain","date":". 01-24-2020, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T07:55:52-08:00","id":1365727,"title":"","content":"I'd probably make the temple of Holy Decouring as an Abyssal Verge, but to me Howard's Rock is firmly in the material world, albeit tainted by a widespread abyssal environmental tilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}